== Implementation (2026-11-06) ==
app/lib/export/fhir_report.dart  buildFhirReport(response, exportedAt) -> Bundle (collection): Genomic Report
  (DiagnosticReport, partial; LOINC 51969-4; GE; test-disclaimer and test-methodology notes; conclusion lists every drug
  with its label), Specimen (VCF sample name as identifier; no Patient), DocumentReference (the uploaded VCF, not
  included), one Genotype per gene called (LOINC 84413-4, value "<gene> <diplotype>"), a not-determined genotype
  observation per capability gene of an Unknown, one Therapeutic Implication per analysed drug (medication text,
  phenotype text, conclusion-string = served CPIC action or the app's unknownExplanation, note "PharmaGuard result:
  <label>", workflow-relatedArtifact citing the served source when a CPIC entry matched). Observations preliminary,
  effectiveDateTime = analysis time. Ids: version-5-shaped UUIDs from sha256(sample|timestamp|key): same response,
  same bundle. crypto ^3.0.7 named in pubspec (already locked through pdf; the lock changes only "direct main").
app/lib/print/summary_pdf.dart  buildSummaryPdf: the HTML summary's text, node for node, in a pdf MultiPage; running
  header on every page; every placed string reported to a sink; onHeader from the function that draws the header.
app/lib/utils/file_download*.dart  one download seam (web blob / io temp file), split like json_export.
app/lib/screens/results_screen.dart  "Download report" (MenuAnchor): "PDF summary (.pdf)", "FHIR Genomics Report
  (.json)"; optional downloader for tests. Printable summary, Export JSON and Copy JSON untouched.
scripts/fhir_validator.json  the pin: validator 7.0.2 (path, bytes, sha256, URL), FHIR 4.0.1, IG
  hl7.fhir.uv.genomics-reporting#3.0.0, terminology server n/a.
scripts/validate_fhir_exports.py  ensure() the pinned jar (fetch_pinned_artifacts: refuse a mismatch), flutter test
  writes the bundles, a positive control (report code removed), one validator run, fail on any error/fatal or an
  unreported bundle, or a control with no error.
scripts/release_status.py  seventh required check "fhir-validation". .github/workflows/test.yml  Java 17 and the same
  script in the Flutter job. app/README.md  the new files and Download report.
Tests: app/test/fhir_report_test.dart (AC2-AC4, 70), summary_pdf_test.dart (AC5, 29), download_report_test.dart (AC6,
  3), export_fixtures_test.dart (writer, 8); support/fixtures.dart shared.

== Design changes found by measurement (logged before commit; acceptance criteria unchanged) ==
1. Not-determined genotypes. Design section 1 put the Genotype profile on them. First validator run on the seven
   bundles: 5 errors, all "Observation.value[x]: minimum required = 1 ... (from genotype|3.0.0)": the profile requires
   a value, and a not-determined genotype has none. They are now the same LOINC 84413-4 observation without claiming the
   profile: dataAbsentReason "unknown", no value, gene as the gene-studied component. Called genotypes keep the profile.
2. PDF fonts. Design section 2 said Newsreader for prose. The independent pypdf check (below) found the prose text layer
   without spaces ("drugschecked", "Itwasproducedbyafinal-year..."): 88/104 HTML nodes found in S1, the misses all
   multi-word prose. The pdf package draws words without space glyphs; a reader infers the gaps, and with a variable
   font it did not. Probes, prose font only changed: PublicSans-Variable 89/104 (S1), also failing; IBMPlexMono-Regular
   104/104 and every fixture complete. The PDF is now all static IBM Plex Mono. A test now requires every PDF font to
   be static (no fvar table); positive control: pointing prose back at Newsreader fails it ("not contains 'fvar'").
3. Found while writing the sabotages: the per-page header check took the page from the MultiPage header callback, not
   from the code that draws the header text, so a header dropped in the callback would have passed if the callback
   still reported. runningHeader(page) now reports from where it draws. SB9-g is that sabotage.
4. Found by SB9-c: the validation script's positive control did `del report["code"]`, so a bundle already missing the
   code crashed the script (exit 1) before the validator ran: red for the wrong reason, which the sabotage harness
   counted as not caught. Now pop(..., None); SB9-c is caught by validator errors.

== How AC3's last sentence is read ==
"An Unknown whose served gene is Unknown gets dataAbsentReason and never a value", with design section 1 (the
not-determined genotype is for "an Unknown drug with a capability gene"): codeine (CYP2D6), S2 clopidogrel (CYP2C19)
and S4 fluorouracil (DPYD) each get a not-determined observation with dataAbsentReason and no value. Ibuprofen has no
gene in the response or in the capability table: it gets no genotype observation, so never a value, and its
Therapeutic Implication derives from the DocumentReference alone. Stated here rather than assumed; the test asserts
exactly this.

