== Release gate, first run on 5c77126 (partb/B9.gate-run1.json, B9.gate-run1.rc): NOT READY ==
rc 1, state not-ready. compatible-bundle passed; backend-tests failed, and the gate stops at the first failed check, so
the other five did not run. The failure: tests/test_phase5a_tooling.py::TestKeyHygiene::
test_exception_sites_are_scrubbed. scripts/validate_fhir_exports.py printed a caught exception as {exc} without
scrub(). The repo's rule: every script that renders an exception scrubs it first, because third-party error text can
carry a secret. My error: before committing B9 I ran the Flutter suite but not the backend suite, where the scripts/
tests live. Fixed (scrub imported from _common, the one print wrapped); the hygiene tests pass (28/28). scripts/ is
outside the scientific core, so the re-bind stands. The full backend suite is rerun before the fix is committed.
Backend suite after the fix (partb/B9.backend-suite.stdout): 1172 collected; 1166 passed, 6 skipped, 0 failed (B8's
six skips; B9 adds no backend test).
